{"title":"Career Roadmap · Radiotherapy Technologist","role":"Radiotherapy Technologist","summary":"A Radiotherapy Technologist is an allied-health professional who supports the delivery of radiation therapy to cancer patients. The role involves patient positioning, treatment setup, radiation equipment operation, treatment verification, radiation-safety procedures, documentation, and close coordination with radiation oncologists, medical physicists, and oncology teams.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Radiotherapy Technologist is an allied-health professional who supports the delivery of radiation therapy to cancer patients. The role involves patient positioning, treatment setup, radiation equipment operation, treatment verification, radiation-safety procedures, documentation, and close coordination with radiation oncologists, medical physicists, and oncology teams."},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, the direct undergraduate pathway should be a recognized program specifically aligned with Radiotherapy Technology / Radiation Therapy Technology / Radiotherapy & Oncology Technology or an equivalent recognized radiation-therapy qualification. A generic BPT, BOT, BMLT, or other allied-health degree does not automatically qualify someone to work as a radiotherapy technologist. Exact eligibility, scope of practice, registration, and employer requirements depend on the recognized qualification and applicable recruitment/regulatory rules."},{"type":"p","text":"The profession combines oncology knowledge + radiation physics + medical technology + patient care + safety. Future technologists will increasingly work with image-guided radiotherapy, adaptive radiotherapy, treatment-planning systems, automation, AI-assisted verification, and increasingly sophisticated radiation-delivery platforms."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build strong foundations in radiotherapy technology, anatomy, oncology, radiation physics, patient positioning, treatment machines, imaging, dosimetry fundamentals, and radiation safety."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Work as a Radiotherapy Technologist and develop expertise in LINACs, IGRT, immobilization, treatment verification, brachytherapy support, and advanced oncology workflows."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Move toward senior technologist, specialist technologist, treatment-unit coordinator, clinical applications, quality assurance, or radiation-technology roles."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Progress into departmental leadership, clinical applications, radiation-technology management, education/training, research, or specialized oncology technology roles."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the UG Degree","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Medical & Radiation Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Build the medical foundation required to understand cancer treatment."},{"type":"h","text":"Core Subjects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Human physiology"},{"text":"Pathology"},{"text":"Basic oncology"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Patient care"},{"text":"Basic pharmacology"},{"text":"Basic microbiology"},{"text":"First aid"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Professional ethics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Foundations"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Atomic structure"},{"text":"Radioactivity"},{"text":"Radiation types"},{"text":"X-rays"},{"text":"Gamma rays"},{"text":"Radiation interaction with matter"},{"text":"Radiation dose"},{"text":"Radiation units"},{"text":"Radiation attenuation"},{"text":"Radiation protection principles"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Basic Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand the purpose and operation of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"X-ray systems"},{"text":"CT scanners"},{"text":"Radiation therapy machines"},{"text":"Treatment simulators"},{"text":"Imaging systems"},{"text":"Patient-monitoring equipment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Radiotherapy Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Move from general medical knowledge into radiation therapy."},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Therapy Equipment"},{"type":"h","text":"Develop familiarity with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Linear accelerators (LINAC)"},{"text":"Cobalt therapy systems"},{"text":"CT simulators"},{"text":"Treatment couches"},{"text":"Immobilization systems"},{"text":"Multileaf collimators"},{"text":"Beam-shaping systems"},{"text":"Portal imaging"},{"text":"On-board imaging"},{"text":"Surface-guided radiation therapy systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient"},{"type":"h","text":"Diagnosis"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Oncology Consultation"},{"type":"h","text":"CT Simulation"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Planning"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Verification"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Delivery"},{"type":"h","text":"Follow-up"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Clinical Radiotherapy Practice"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop practical competency in the treatment workflow."},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Positioning"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Reproducible positioning"},{"text":"Immobilization"},{"text":"Head-and-neck positioning"},{"text":"Thoracic positioning"},{"text":"Breast positioning"},{"text":"Pelvic positioning"},{"text":"Abdominal positioning"},{"text":"Extremity positioning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Immobilization Devices"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Thermoplastic masks"},{"text":"Vacuum cushions"},{"text":"Breast boards"},{"text":"Headrests"},{"text":"Pelvic immobilization"},{"text":"Customized positioning aids"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The objective is accurate and reproducible positioning throughout the treatment course."},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Techniques"},{"type":"h","text":"Become familiar with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"2D radiotherapy"},{"text":"3D conformal radiotherapy (3D-CRT)"},{"text":"IMRT"},{"text":"VMAT"},{"text":"IGRT"},{"text":"SRS"},{"text":"SBRT"},{"text":"Electron therapy"},{"text":"Total body irradiation fundamentals"},{"text":"Brachytherapy workflows"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Understand the difference between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Treatment planning","verification","delivery"]},{"type":"p","text":"rather than treating these as a single process."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Advanced Clinical Practice"},{"type":"p","text":"The final year should focus heavily on supervised clinical exposure."},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"LINAC workflow"},{"text":"IGRT"},{"text":"Treatment verification"},{"text":"Image matching"},{"text":"Daily setup verification"},{"text":"Treatment documentation"},{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"Emergency procedures"},{"text":"Quality assurance"},{"text":"Brachytherapy assistance"},{"text":"Oncology patient communication"},{"text":"Clinical workflow management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Oncology Knowledge"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong technologist should understand the major cancer sites treated using radiotherapy."},{"type":"h","text":"Major Treatment Areas"},{"type":"table","header":["Cancer Site","Important Knowledge"],"rows":[[{"text":"Brain"},{"text":"Immobilization, stereotactic treatment concepts"}],[{"text":"Head & Neck"},{"text":"Masks, image guidance, organ-at-risk considerations"}],[{"text":"Breast"},{"text":"Positioning, respiratory-management concepts"}],[{"text":"Lung"},{"text":"Motion management, SBRT concepts"}],[{"text":"Prostate"},{"text":"Pelvic positioning, IGRT"}],[{"text":"Cervix"},{"text":"External beam + brachytherapy workflow"}],[{"text":"Rectum"},{"text":"Pelvic setup and image guidance"}],[{"text":"Spine"},{"text":"Immobilization and stereotactic concepts"}],[{"text":"Bone"},{"text":"Palliative radiation workflows"}],[{"text":"Paediatric cancers"},{"text":"Specialized immobilization and patient communication"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Physics & Dosimetry Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Radiotherapy technologists do not replace medical physicists, but they need sufficient physics knowledge to understand safe treatment delivery."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiation dose"},{"text":"Dose rate"},{"text":"Beam energy"},{"text":"Beam profiles"},{"text":"Percentage depth dose"},{"text":"Tissue-phantom ratio"},{"text":"Monitor units"},{"text":"Field size"},{"text":"Beam modifiers"},{"text":"Wedges"},{"text":"MLCs"},{"text":"Photon beams"},{"text":"Electron beams"},{"text":"Dose distributions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important Principle"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Oncologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Prescribes Treatment"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Physicist / Dosimetry Team"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Planning & Verification"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiotherapy Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Accurate Treatment Setup & Delivery"},{"type":"p","text":"The exact division of responsibilities varies by institution and jurisdiction."},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Safety"},{"type":"p","text":"Radiation safety should become one of the strongest competencies."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ALARA principle"},{"text":"Time"},{"text":"Distance"},{"text":"Shielding"},{"text":"Radiation monitoring"},{"text":"Controlled areas"},{"text":"Warning systems"},{"text":"Radiation surveys"},{"text":"Personal dosimetry"},{"text":"Pregnancy-related radiation precautions"},{"text":"Equipment safety"},{"text":"Emergency procedures"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Safety Principle"},{"type":"h","text":"Minimize Exposure"},{"type":"h","text":"Time ↓"},{"type":"h","text":"Distance ↑"},{"type":"h","text":"Shielding ↑"},{"type":"h","text":"Safe Radiation Environment"},{"type":"h","text":"Imaging & Image-Guided Radiotherapy"},{"type":"p","text":"Modern radiotherapy is increasingly image-driven."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CT simulation"},{"text":"Cone-beam CT"},{"text":"kV imaging"},{"text":"MV imaging"},{"text":"Image registration"},{"text":"Image matching"},{"text":"Patient setup verification"},{"text":"Motion assessment"},{"text":"Surface imaging"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important Skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Recognizing positioning errors"},{"text":"Identifying anatomical landmarks"},{"text":"Understanding image-registration concepts"},{"text":"Escalating significant deviations to the appropriate clinical team"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Brachytherapy Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"Develop foundational knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Intracavitary brachytherapy"},{"text":"Interstitial brachytherapy"},{"text":"Applicators"},{"text":"Treatment rooms"},{"text":"Afterloading systems"},{"text":"Source handling principles"},{"text":"Patient preparation"},{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"Emergency procedures"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Common applications include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cervical cancer"},{"text":"Endometrial cancer"},{"text":"Prostate cancer"},{"text":"Selected breast cancers"},{"text":"Other site-specific treatments"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Because brachytherapy involves radioactive sources, strict institutional radiation-safety procedures are essential."},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Planning Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with the concepts behind:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Treatment planning systems (TPS)"},{"text":"Contouring"},{"text":"Dose calculation"},{"text":"Dose-volume histograms"},{"text":"Treatment fields"},{"text":"Beam arrangements"},{"text":"Plan verification"},{"text":"Image-guided workflows"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Examples of systems encountered in the industry may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Eclipse"},{"text":"RayStation"},{"text":"Monaco"},{"text":"Pinnacle"},{"text":"Other institution-specific TPS platforms"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The goal at undergraduate level is workflow understanding and supervised clinical competency, not independent treatment-plan approval."},{"type":"h","text":"Digital & Data Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"A modern radiotherapy technologist should develop basic digital competence."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Clinical documentation"},{"text":"Electronic health records"},{"text":"Oncology information systems"},{"text":"Treatment-management systems"},{"text":"Basic SQL"},{"text":"Data quality"},{"text":"Clinical dashboards"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful Advanced Skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python fundamentals"},{"text":"Data visualization"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Image-processing fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI in Radiotherapy"},{"type":"p","text":"AI is becoming increasingly relevant to oncology workflows."},{"type":"h","text":"Understand applications such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Automated image segmentation"},{"text":"Auto-contouring"},{"text":"Treatment-plan optimization"},{"text":"Image registration"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Treatment verification"},{"text":"Motion detection"},{"text":"Adaptive radiotherapy"},{"text":"Predictive analytics"},{"text":"Workflow automation"},{"text":"Quality assurance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"A useful learning pathway is:"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiotherapy"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Data"},{"type":"h","text":"Python"},{"type":"h","text":"Image Processing"},{"type":"h","text":"Machine Learning"},{"type":"h","text":"AI-assisted Radiotherapy"},{"type":"p","text":"AI should be treated as a clinical decision-support and workflow technology, not as a replacement for qualified clinical professionals."},{"type":"h","text":"Quality Assurance"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn the purpose of QA in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"LINAC operation"},{"text":"Imaging systems"},{"text":"Treatment delivery"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"Treatment verification"},{"text":"Documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Understand concepts such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Machine performance checks"},{"text":"Calibration principles"},{"text":"Output consistency"},{"text":"Imaging QA"},{"text":"MLC verification"},{"text":"Treatment-delivery verification"},{"text":"Incident reporting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Detailed machine QA and calibration responsibilities are generally assigned to appropriately qualified medical physics personnel."},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Project Ideas"}]},{"heading":"AI-Assisted Patient Position Verification","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop a prototype that identifies positioning differences between reference and treatment images."}]},{"heading":"Radiation Therapy Treatment Workflow Dashboard","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Create a dashboard tracking:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patients"},{"text":"Treatment fractions"},{"text":"Treatment status"},{"text":"Machine utilization"},{"text":"Missed sessions"},{"text":"Workflow delays"}]}]},{"heading":"Image-Guided Radiotherapy Analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Study image-registration accuracy using anonymized imaging datasets."}]},{"heading":"Radiation Safety Monitoring System","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop a conceptual digital system for tracking:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Staff radiation exposure"},{"text":"Safety checks"},{"text":"Equipment inspections"},{"text":"Incident reports"}]}]},{"heading":"End-to-End Radiotherapy Workflow Project","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Cancer Diagnosis"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Oncology Consultation"},{"type":"h","text":"CT Simulation"},{"type":"h","text":"Immobilization"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Planning"},{"type":"h","text":"Verification"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Delivery"},{"type":"h","text":"QA & Documentation"},{"type":"p","text":"Document the role of the radiotherapy technologist at every stage."},{"type":"h","text":"Internship & Clinical Training Strategy"},{"type":"p","text":"Clinical exposure is particularly important for this career."},{"type":"h","text":"Priority 1 — Cancer Hospitals"},{"type":"h","text":"Seek training in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiation oncology departments"},{"text":"Cancer institutes"},{"text":"Comprehensive oncology hospitals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Priority 2 — Radiation Therapy Units"},{"type":"h","text":"Gain exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"LINAC"},{"text":"CT simulation"},{"text":"IGRT"},{"text":"Treatment setup"},{"text":"Brachytherapy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Priority 3 — Medical Physics Department"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"Machine QA"},{"text":"Dosimetry concepts"},{"text":"Equipment quality control"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Priority 4 — Oncology Technology Companies"},{"type":"h","text":"Explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiotherapy equipment"},{"text":"Treatment-planning software"},{"text":"Oncology information systems"},{"text":"Clinical applications"}]}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After completing the appropriate recognized qualification and required clinical training, potential roles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiotherapy Technologist"},{"text":"Radiation Therapy Technologist"},{"text":"Radiation Oncology Technologist"},{"text":"Radiotherapy Technician"},{"text":"Oncology Technology Assistant"},{"text":"Treatment Delivery Technologist"},{"text":"IGRT Technologist"},{"text":"Brachytherapy Technologist"},{"text":"Radiotherapy Department Assistant"},{"text":"Clinical Applications Trainee"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Exact job titles and eligibility vary by institution and recruitment notification."},{"type":"h","text":"Employer Skill Matrix"},{"type":"table","header":["Employer Type","Most Valuable Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Cancer Hospital"},{"text":"LINAC + patient setup + IGRT"}],[{"text":"Oncology Institute"},{"text":"Radiotherapy workflow + oncology"}],[{"text":"Government Hospital"},{"text":"Clinical competency + documentation + safety"}],[{"text":"Private Cancer Centre"},{"text":"LINAC + IGRT + patient communication"}],[{"text":"Radiation Technology Company"},{"text":"Equipment + applications + troubleshooting"}],[{"text":"Research Centre"},{"text":"Radiation physics + data + research"}],[{"text":"Academic Institution"},{"text":"Clinical expertise + teaching"}],[{"text":"Healthcare Technology Company"},{"text":"Oncology workflow + digital systems"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize recognized or institutionally relevant training rather than collecting certificates."},{"type":"h","text":"Core"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiation safety training"},{"text":"Basic Life Support (BLS)"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Patient safety"},{"text":"Clinical documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiotherapy technology"},{"text":"LINAC operation"},{"text":"IGRT"},{"text":"Treatment-planning fundamentals"},{"text":"Radiation oncology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Medical imaging fundamentals"},{"text":"Healthcare data analytics"}]}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Depending on eligibility and institutional offerings, possible postgraduate directions include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiotherapy / Radiation Sciences"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc Radiotherapy Technology"},{"text":"M.Sc Radiation Therapy"},{"text":"M.Sc Medical Radiation Technology"},{"text":"Advanced oncology technology programs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc Medical Technology"},{"text":"M.Sc Healthcare Technology"},{"text":"Master of Public Health"},{"text":"Healthcare Management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medical Imaging"},{"text":"Health Informatics"},{"text":"Healthcare Data Analytics"},{"text":"Biomedical Technology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"h","text":"For long-term research careers:"},{"type":"h","text":"Relevant UG"},{"type":"h","text":"PG / Specialized Training"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Experience"},{"type":"h","text":"M.Phil / PhD where applicable"},{"type":"h","text":"Oncology Technology Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Specific postgraduate eligibility must be checked against the university's admission requirements."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Specializations"},{"type":"p","text":"After gaining clinical experience, specialization can develop in:"},{"type":"h","text":"1. LINAC Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on advanced external-beam radiotherapy workflows."},{"type":"h","text":"2. IGRT Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on image-guided treatment verification."},{"type":"h","text":"3. Brachytherapy Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on brachytherapy workflows and patient setup."},{"type":"h","text":"4. SRS/SBRT Technologist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on highly precise stereotactic treatments."},{"type":"h","text":"5. Paediatric Radiotherapy Technologist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on specialized positioning and paediatric oncology workflows."},{"type":"h","text":"6. Clinical Applications Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Work with radiotherapy equipment manufacturers and hospitals."},{"type":"h","text":"7. Radiation Technology Educator"},{"type":"p","text":"Move toward teaching and clinical training."},{"type":"h","text":"8. Oncology Technology Researcher"},{"type":"p","text":"Work on imaging, automation, AI, treatment technology, or workflow optimization."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"UG Radiotherapy Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiotherapy Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Radiotherapy Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Chief / Lead Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiotherapy Department Coordinator"},{"type":"h","text":"Alternative Technology Path"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiotherapy Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Applications Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Applications Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Technology Manager"},{"type":"h","text":"Oncology Technology Leadership"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Path"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiotherapy Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"PG / Specialized Training"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Scientist"},{"type":"h","text":"Oncology Technology Research Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging Technologies"},{"type":"p","text":"The profession is likely to be increasingly influenced by:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted contouring"},{"text":"Automated treatment planning"},{"text":"Adaptive radiotherapy"},{"text":"Surface-guided radiation therapy"},{"text":"Real-time image guidance"},{"text":"4D imaging"},{"text":"Motion tracking"},{"text":"MRI-guided radiotherapy"},{"text":"Proton therapy"},{"text":"Heavy-ion therapy"},{"text":"Robotic patient positioning"},{"text":"Digital twins for treatment workflows"},{"text":"Cloud-based oncology information systems"},{"text":"Predictive analytics"},{"text":"Automated QA"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Future Skill Combination"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiotherapy"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Physics"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Health"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"AI"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Safety"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Radiotherapy Professional"},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"Oncology"},{"text":"Patient care"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Clinical communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Radiotherapy"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"LINAC"},{"text":"CT simulation"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Immobilization"},{"text":"3D-CRT"},{"text":"IMRT"},{"text":"VMAT"},{"text":"IGRT"},{"text":"SRS/SBRT fundamentals"},{"text":"Brachytherapy fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Safety"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiation protection"},{"text":"ALARA"},{"text":"Personal dosimetry"},{"text":"Emergency procedures"},{"text":"Safety documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Treatment-management systems"},{"text":"Treatment-planning workflow"},{"text":"Medical imaging"},{"text":"Oncology information systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Basic SQL"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Medical image processing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Teamwork"},{"text":"Patient communication"},{"text":"Accuracy"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Incident reporting"},{"text":"Clinical ethics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong graduate should be able to demonstrate:"},{"type":"h","text":"Recognized Radiotherapy Qualification"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"LINAC Workflow Knowledge"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Positioning"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"IGRT Fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Safety"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Oncology Knowledge"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Brachytherapy Fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Healthcare Skills"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"AI/Imaging Awareness"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Job-Ready Radiotherapy Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["Recognized Radiotherapy/Radiation Therapy Technology degree","extensive cancer-hospital clinical training","LINAC + IGRT + radiation safety","advanced radiotherapy exposure","specialization in IGRT/SRS-SBRT/brachytherapy/clinical applications","PG or technology/research pathway"],"label":"Best pathway"},{"type":"p","text":"The most important differentiator is strong supervised clinical competence on actual radiotherapy workflows, supported by radiation-safety knowledge and increasingly strong digital/imaging skills."}]}]}